          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Lorck directly avows love for Constance and immediately emphasizes that the declaration is serious and deeper than he himself had understood. Its dominant force is presenting his loving emotional state as true.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The declaration is integrated into a solemn offer of himself, his life and his soul, rather than merely accompanied by an unrelated promise. In this occurrence, “I love you” grounds and affirms his readiness to enter a comprehensive romantic bond if Constance accepts him. The undertaking is substantial but vaguely defined and conditional on her acceptance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Nej, uf nej,\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"reason\":\"Although Lorck is emotionally agitated, the focal words form a deliberate, intelligible avowal and appeal after he has pressed Constance for an answer. They are not represented as a reflex-like cry or uncontrolled expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Lorck korsede Armene paa Brystet, og\\nbetragtede hende stift.\"},{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.82,\"reason\":\"No additional core force needs a separate category. The avowal is covered by T and its participation in the self-offering by P. The ensuing question soliciting acceptance is a distinct directive component of the larger turn, not an additional core force of the marked words themselves.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"vil du ikke ta imod det?\"},{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During a private conversation about love, Lorck reveals that his long-standing infatuation concerns Constance. After kneeling, urging her to yield to him, and reacting threateningly when she resists, he makes the focal declaration as part of a serious offer of himself and asks for acceptance. Constance immediately refuses and withdraws, so the scene is coercively pressured rather than mutually affectionate.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Lorck offers Constance himself, his life and his soul, thereby affirming readiness for an extensive but unspecified romantic undertaking. The focal avowal helps enact and solemnize that offer rather than merely reporting an emotion beside it. Constance’s “Nej, uf nej” is an immediate rejection, so no mutually accepted bond is created.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages explicitly identify the work as Amalie Skram’s Constance Ring. No remembered plot facts beyond the supplied evidence were used.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly represents Lorck as affected—his voice shakes, he acts nervously, and he describes a consuming passion—but it cannot conclusively establish sincerity or the precise obligations he intended by offering his life and soul. His coercive conduct affects the interaction and uptake but does not by itself negate either the avowal’s truth-presenting form or its undertaking force.\"}"
        }
